# /mobile-porter — Per-game mobile touch audit and fixes

This rule triggers the **mobile-porter** skill. Read `.claude/skills/mobile-porter/SKILL.md` and follow it strictly.

## What this does

- Takes a **game slug** (e.g. `asteroids`, `tetris`) — **one game per session**
- Audits touch play against SPEC 10 and `mobile-game-checklist.md`
- Fixes gaps in engine API, player wiring, canvas cleanup, and touch CSS
- Verifies desktop keyboard has no regressions
- Updates inventory in `references/mobile-porter/coverage-log.md`

## What this does NOT do

- Modify landing, library, hall of fame, about, or other non-game pages
- Audit or fix all playables in one go
- Write specs or mark them as `Aprobado`
- Implement PWA, native fullscreen, or haptic feedback
- Touch placeholders until integrated (unless explicitly requested)

## Supporting files

- `.claude/skills/mobile-porter/SKILL.md` — five-phase workflow and hard rules
- `.claude/skills/mobile-porter/touch-integration-guide.md` — wiring patterns and constants
- `.claude/skills/mobile-porter/mobile-game-checklist.md` — per-game audit checklist
- `specs/10-controles-tactiles-movil.md` — canonical touch play spec
- `references/mobile-porter/coverage-log.md` — mobile coverage inventory (read at start, update at end)

## Workflow summary

1. **Context** — read `coverage-log.md`, SPEC 10, target game touch files
2. **Confirm game** — single slug from argument or user prompt
3. **Audit** — walk `mobile-game-checklist.md` for the slug
4. **Fix** — minimal diffs in engine, player, canvas, CSS if gaps found
5. **Verify** — lint + manual desktop/touch check on `/play/{slug}`
6. **Persist** — update game row + append session in `coverage-log.md`, then **STOP**

## Subagent

For a clean context, delegate to [`.cursor/agents/mobile-porter.md`](.cursor/agents/mobile-porter.md) when the user explicitly asks for the `@mobile-porter` subagent.

## Example invocations

```
@mobile-porter tetris
@mobile-porter asteroids
@mobile-porter audit
```

## Handoff

After `@spec-impl` for a new game → `@mobile-porter {slug}` to wire touch controls.
